=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A thorough end-to-end investigation of the simple_bgp topology finds no fault anywhere in the network. Every layer was checked:

**Data plane**: A live ping from pc1 (195.11.14.2) to pc2 (200.1.1.2) returned 4/4 packets with 0% loss and a TTL of 62, which is exactly right for a two-hop eBGP path.

**Routing**: Both routers have correct, fully-installed routes. router1 holds a BGP-learned route `B>* 200.1.1.0/24 via 193.10.11.2` and router2 holds `B>* 195.11.14.0/24 via 193.10.11.1`. No routes are missing.

**BGP session**: The eBGP session between router1 (AS 1) and router2 (AS 2) over the 193.10.11.0/24 inter-router link has been continuously established for over two minutes, exchanging keepalives every 60 seconds. The BGP log shows a clean startup, correct UPDATE exchanges, and no resets or NOTIFICATION messages.

**Physical layer**: Both eth0 inter-router interfaces report `UP/LOWER_UP` with standard MTU 1500 — no carrier drop, no error counts, nothing suggesting a cable or link fault.

**End-host configuration**: pc1 and pc2 both have correct IP addresses and default gateways pointing to their respective routers.

**Root cause**: There is no fault. The operations team's assertion that "the line between the two buildings went down" is incorrect. The network has been healthy since lab start and end-to-end reachability is fully confirmed right now. No corrective action is needed.
=== END ===